From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 05:11:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 163/190] Sega CD: drive letters a TOS user would expect

A: and B: are the floppy slots. On a TOS machine that means removable
media, and C: onward means storage that cannot leave the machine. This
port had it exactly inverted: the two things a person can physically
remove -- the cartridge and the disc -- were on C: and D:, and the two
that cannot -- a ramdisk in cartridge ROM and eight kilobytes soldered
inside the console -- were the floppies.

So they swap. The cartridge takes A: and the disc B:; the ramdisk takes
C: and the console's backup RAM D:. Nothing about the devices changes,
only which layer of the block system each is reached through.

The cartridge is on A: rather than the disc because A: is the drive the
desktop asks about first, and cartridge save RAM answers instantly
where a disc has to spin up.

The floppy path addresses through segacd_floprw()'s sixteen-sectors-to-
a-track geometry, which was already what flop_detect_drive() set. A WORD
of track at sixteen sectors reaches 268 MB, comfortably past either
device. The bodies that used to be inline there are now segacd_ramdisk_*
and segacd_bram_* on the two buses, which are renamed to say what they
carry: BRAM_BUS and RAMDISK_BUS. The ramdisk is listed first in
majors[], and first is C:.

And that is the point of the whole rearrangement: DEFAULT_BOOTDEV is C:,
unmodified upstream EmuTOS, and it is now correct. The override added
for this machine is gone. C: is the ramdisk, which is the system drive
-- always present, in ROM, holding EMUDESK.INF and EMUICON.RSC and the
programs -- which is what C: means on a TOS machine.

flop_mediach() stops being a constant, because B: is a disc and a disc
can be swapped. The FMTTEST diagnostic targets D: through
GET_UNITNUM(BRAM_BUS,0) rather than B: through unit 1, since B: cannot
be written at all now.

Verified in the emulator: all four drives mount with the new letters,
the desktop finds its icon files on C: with no override, and CDTEST on
B: reaches Fopen and reads back the opening bytes of the file that is
on the disc.
